Let `arch/rlx` offer gpiolib, so a `gpio_chip` can be registered at all.

WHY THIS EXISTS.  `R5-4` writes `rtl819x-gpio` as a real `struct gpio_chip`.
On this tree it could not be built, and that is a measurement rather than a
reading of the Kconfig files:

  `drivers/gpio/Kconfig:27` -- `menuconfig GPIOLIB` -- carries
  `depends on ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB || ARCH_REQUIRE_GPIOLIB`.  Both of
  those are declared in that same file (lines 5 and 15) as promptless bools
  meant to be `select`ed by an architecture.  `arch/rlx/Kconfig` selects
  neither.  `arch/mips/Kconfig` and `arch/x86/Kconfig` -- both present in this
  drop -- do.

量 2026-09-06, thirty-seventh segment, cell `r54gate`, `--target none` so
nothing was compiled.  The `.config` of `ea6ee537` (the image that booted
eleven times that day) had three lines appended and `make oldconfig
< /dev/null` was run on a freshly staged tree:

    CONFIG_GPIOLIB=y                      -> dropped, absent from the output
    CONFIG_GENERIC_GPIO=y                 -> dropped
    CONFIG_ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB=y   -> dropped

THE CONTROL IS WHAT MAKES THAT MEAN ANYTHING.  A run in which the appended
lines never reached `oldconfig` at all -- wrong path, wrong tree, a copy that
did not happen -- prints exactly the same three results.  So a fourth line was
edited in the same file in the same run, and it had to come out CHANGED:
`# CONFIG_SWAP is not set` was flipped to `CONFIG_SWAP=y`, whose prompt is
satisfied by `CONFIG_MMU=y` and `CONFIG_BLOCK=y` in that same file.  量: it
survived.  The whole diff between input and output is five lines -- the three
drops, and the two halves of the `.config`'s own datestamp.

量 `K6`, cell `r54gate2`, the same procedure with this patch applied: all
three lines now SURVIVE -- `CONFIG_GPIOLIB=y`, and with it
`CONFIG_GENERIC_GPIO=y` (gpiolib `select`s it) and
`CONFIG_ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB=y`.

WHY `OPTIONAL` AND NOT `REQUIRE`.  `ARCH_REQUIRE_GPIOLIB` `select`s `GPIOLIB`,
which would turn gpiolib on for every build of this arch whether or not
anything asked.  `ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB` only makes the menu entry
reachable and leaves it off.  So this patch on its own changes nothing that is
built -- and the first draft of this paragraph said that on one line of
evidence and was wrong about the line.

量 `K7`, cell `r54gate3`, this patch applied and the GPIO lines NOT in the
input `.config`.  The prediction was that the output would gain the single
line `# CONFIG_GPIOLIB is not set`.  🔴 **It gains TWO**: kconfig also writes
out the symbol this patch selects.  The whole diff against the input is four
lines -- the two halves of the datestamp, plus

    CONFIG_ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB=y
    # CONFIG_GPIOLIB is not set

So the claim has to be carried by the second line meaning nothing to a build,
which is a different measurement and was taken rather than assumed.  量 over
the staged tree: `CONFIG_ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB` appears in **0**
`Makefile`/`Kbuild` files and **0** `.c`/`.h` files; its only occurrences
anywhere are its own declaration, the `depends on` line in the same file, and
`arch/x86/Kconfig:29`.  The positive control is the same two greps for
`CONFIG_GPIOLIB`, which return **1** and **10** -- so the greps can find a
consumer, and for this symbol there is none.

What turns gpiolib on is `config/rlxfw-kernel.delta`, in a separate line with
its own reason, and that line can be removed without touching this file.

WHOSE CHANGE IT IS.  The mechanism is mainline's own and this patch is its
documented use.  `drivers/gpio/Kconfig:5-14`, verbatim in this drop:

    config ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB
        bool
        help
          Select this config option from the architecture Kconfig, if
          it is possible to use gpiolib on the architecture, but let the
          user decide whether to actually build it or not.

Nothing is introduced.  One `select` is added beside the `select EMBEDDED`
that is already there, on `config MIPS` -- `arch/rlx`'s arch-wide `default y`
symbol.

🔴 **THE PRECEDENT IS x86, NOT mips, and the first draft of this file said
mips.**  量, every Kconfig reference in this drop:
`arch/x86/Kconfig:29` is the ONLY `select ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB` in the
tree, and it is arch-wide.  `arch/mips/Kconfig` selects the other symbol,
`ARCH_REQUIRE_GPIOLIB`, and does it **per board** (lines 601 and 884), with
four more boards selecting `GENERIC_GPIO` directly and supplying their own
`gpio_*` bodies.  x86's shape is the one this patch copies, and it is the
right one here for a stated reason rather than by convenience: the claim being
made is about the ARCHITECTURE -- `arch/rlx` has the header and the
`#ifdef CONFIG_GPIOLIB` branch, so gpiolib is possible on it -- and not about
what this one board needs.  Whether the RTL8196E board turns it on is the
`.config`'s business.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES NOT ESTABLISH.  That a gpiochip will link.
`arch/rlx/include/asm/mach-generic/gpio.h:16-17` declares `gpio_to_irq()` and
`irq_to_gpio()` **outside** the `CONFIG_GPIOLIB` guard, and `arch/rlx` defines
neither.  Nothing in the built set is known to call them; if something does,
the failure is at link time and loud.  That is `R5-4`'s risk to carry, not
this patch's to fix.

THE DIRECTORY NAME IS NOW WRONG FOR THREE OF ITS FIVE FILES.  `0001` (perl
5.22) and `0004` (GNU Make 4.3's `\#`) are host compatibility in the strict
sense.  `0002`, `0003` and this one are not: they are declared source changes
to the vendor tree, which is what `tools/rlxfw-kbuild.sh:321-324` already
calls this directory in its own comment.  The rename is carried forward in
`PROGRESS.md` rather than done in the segment that widened it again.

--- a/arch/rlx/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/rlx/Kconfig
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
     bool
     default y
     select EMBEDDED
+    select ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB
 
 config TRAD_SIGNALS
     bool
